"We present a computational framework under the following settings: (a) ...; (b) access to the database is enabled through a getNext() [43] interface ...; and (c) ... problem of designing anytime algorithms for computing AFDs in a relation considering three different error measures [21], where the actual records are read one by one, or in small batches. Anytime algorithms [2,47] are designed to progressively improve the quality of their results as more computation time becomes available, while still being capable of returning a valid (though possibly suboptimal) solution if interrupted at any stage. Our proposed algorithms fall within a subclass of anytime algorithms that begin producing outputs after reading only a small portion of the data."

